# What a failing call leaves behind on the way out. A .err case records the
# rendered error and throws stdout away, so the half of the promise under
# **map, filter and reduce** that says the earlier elements already ran can
# only be watched from here, where a real terminal sees both streams.
-e 'print(map([1, 2, 3], fn(x) { print(x) + 1 }))'
-e 'print(reduce([1, 2, 3], fn(a, x) { print(x) + 1 }, 0))'
